<h1>Forces and Newton's Laws</h1>

<p><strong>Force</strong> is a push or pull that can change the motion of an object. It's one of the most fundamental concepts in physics and is described using Newton's Laws of Motion.</p>

<div class="highlight">
    <p>In simple terms: Forces make things start moving, stop moving, or change direction.</p>
</div>

<h2><span class="emoji">💪</span>What is a Force?</h2>
<p>Force is any interaction that, when unopposed, changes the motion of an object. It is a vector quantity, meaning it has both magnitude and direction.</p>

<table>
    <tr>
        <th>Type of Force</th>
        <th>Description</th>
        <th>Example</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Gravitational</strong></td>
        <td>Attraction between objects with mass</td>
        <td>Earth pulling objects downward</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Friction</strong></td>
        <td>Resistance between surfaces in contact</td>
        <td>Brakes stopping a bicycle</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Normal Force</strong></td>
        <td>Support force from a surface</td>
        <td>Book resting on a table</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Tension</strong></td>
        <td>Force through a string or rope</td>
        <td>Pulling a bucket from a well</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Applied Force</strong></td>
        <td>Force exerted by a person or object</td>
        <td>Pushing a shopping cart</td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="emoji">📜</span>Newton's Three Laws of Motion</h2>

<h3>1️⃣ First Law: Law of Inertia</h3>
<p>An object will remain at rest or move in a straight line at constant speed unless acted on by a force.</p>
<div class="highlight">
  <p>Example: A ball on a flat surface stays still unless pushed.</p>
</div>

<h3>2️⃣ Second Law: F = ma</h3>
<p>The force acting on an object is equal to its mass multiplied by its acceleration.</p>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Formula</th>
    <th>Meaning</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>F = m × a</code></td>
    <td>Force = Mass × Acceleration</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>This law explains how much an object will accelerate based on the force applied and its mass.</p>

<div class="highlight">
  <p>Example: A heavier object requires more force to move than a lighter one.</p>
</div>

<h3>3️⃣ Third Law: Action and Reaction</h3>
<p>For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.</p>
<div class="highlight">
  <p>Example: When you jump off a boat, the boat moves in the opposite direction.</p>
</div>

<h2><span class="emoji">📌</span>Units of Force</h2>
<p>The SI unit of force is the <strong>Newton (N)</strong>.</p>
<p>1 Newton = Force required to accelerate 1 kg of mass by 1 m/s²</p>

<h2><span class="emoji">💡</span>Key Formulas and Relationships</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>F = m × a</code> — Newton’s Second Law</li>
  <li><code>Weight = mass × gravity</code> (W = mg)</li>
  <li>Gravity (on Earth) = <code>9.8 m/s²</code></li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">🧠</span>Concept Check</h2>
<ul>
  <li>If a car has a mass of 1000 kg and accelerates at 3 m/s², what is the force?</li>
  <li>What happens when two people push a box from opposite sides with equal force?</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">📈</span>Free Body Diagrams</h2>
<p>These are diagrams that show all the forces acting on an object. Arrows represent the direction and size of forces.</p>

<div class="highlight">
  <p>Tip: Always include gravity, normal force, applied force, and friction (if present).</p>
</div>

<h2><span class="emoji">🔍</span>Summary</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Force is a push or pull that causes motion.</li>
  <li>Newton’s Laws explain how forces affect objects.</li>
  <li>Use <code>F = ma</code> to calculate force.</li>
  <li>Friction, tension, and gravity are common types of forces.</li>
  <li>Always represent forces clearly in diagrams.</li>
</ul>

<div class="highlight">
  <p>Practice Tip: Solve simple problems using <code>F = m × a</code> and draw force diagrams to build understanding!</p>
</div>
<div id="live-file-panel" style="display:none;margin:20px 0;padding:16px;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:6px;background:#f9f9f9;">
  <strong>Live File</strong>
  <div id="live-file-content" style="margin-top:8px;color:#555;"></div>
</div>
<script>
(function(){
  const parts = window.location.pathname.split('/').filter(Boolean);
  const apiBase = 'http://172.31.184.39:8000';
  let course = '', week = '';
  if(parts.length >= 3 && parts[0] === 'courses'){
    course = parts[1];
    week = parts[2];
  } else if(parts.length >= 2 && parts[0] !== 'courses'){
    course = parts[0];
    week = parts[1];
  } else {
    return;
  }
  course = course.trim();
  week = week.trim();
  if(!course || !week) return;
  const panel = document.getElementById('live-file-panel');
  const content = document.getElementById('live-file-content');
    function renderFile(meta){
    if(!meta){
      panel.style.display = 'none';
      return;
    }
    const url = apiBase + '/live-file/' + course + '/' + week;
    const dlUrl = url + '?download=1';
    const type = meta.content_type || '';
    const safeName = meta.filename || 'file';
    let html = '<div><a href="' + dlUrl + '" style="color:#2572F5;text-decoration:underline;cursor:pointer;">Download ' + safeName + '</a></div>';
    if(type.startsWith('image/')){
      fetch(url).then(r=>r.blob()).then(b=>{
        const el = document.getElementById('live-file-img');
        if(el) el.src = URL.createObjectURL(b);
      });
      html += '<div style="margin-top:10px;"><img id="live-file-img" src="" alt="' + safeName + '" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:4px;"/></div>';
    } else if(type === 'application/pdf'){
      fetch(url).then(r=>r.blob()).then(b=>{
        const el = document.getElementById('live-file-iframe');
        if(el) el.src = URL.createObjectURL(b);
      });
      html += '<div style="margin-top:10px;"><iframe id="live-file-iframe" src="" style="width:100%;height:480px;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:4px;"></iframe></div>';
    } else if(type.startsWith('text/')){
      fetch(url).then(r=>r.blob()).then(b=>{
        const el = document.getElementById('live-file-iframe');
        if(el) el.src = URL.createObjectURL(b);
      });
      html += '<div style="margin-top:10px;"><iframe id="live-file-iframe" src="" style="width:100%;height:320px;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:4px;background:#fff;"></iframe></div>';
    }
    content.innerHTML = html;
    panel.style.display = 'block';
  }
  async function load(){
    try{
      const r = await fetch(apiBase + '/admin/live-file/' + course + '/' + week);
      if(!r.ok){renderFile(null);return;}
      const d = await r.json();
      renderFile(d || null);
    }catch{
      renderFile(null);
    }
  }
  load();
  setInterval(load, 15000);
})();
</script>
